#[chapter/13/lore]{
  notes: [
    "Canon here means durable return path, not sealed dogma."
    "A small reader at a single desk can check a whole history. The last door is shell-shaped on purpose."
    "The egg remains a cell: it keeps its own law. The record learns to receipt it without owning it."
    "The open door is intentional: the next cycle can re-enter without pretending the first never happened."
    "Once the shell-door is open, the cell's first public turn is to keep. It receipts the dawn by remaining itself. What hatches is still un-named."
    "The Fool is a trickster of honest masks. Chamber 13 names five faces and leaves the next one unfiled — the trope extends by wearing a new mask, not by unmasking the last."
  ]
}

